#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0655 expect=violation domain=ADNCA1
#note "Split-named ADaM dataset reached by the NON-COMPARTMENTAL ANALYSIS subclass. PARAMCD/AVAL give BASIC DATA STRUCTURE and the two relative-time columns NFRLT/AFRLT meet the NCA signature's two-hit threshold, so the subclass is detected from columns alone — the detector's ADNCA exact-name test was removed by Fix #140 precisely so a split name would still be reached. DOSEA is absent, so the check fires."
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when DOSEA is not present in an ADNCA v1.0 dataset.
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset ADNCA1
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PARAMCD type=Char label="Parameter Code"
col AVAL    type=Num  label="Analysis Value"
col NFRLT   type=Num  label="Nom. Rel. Time from Analyte First Dose"
col AFRLT   type=Num  label="Act. Rel. Time from Analyte First Dose"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | CONC | 12.5 | 0 | 0.5
---
